      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We start by using the given information about the arithmetic mean and geometric mean of $x$ and $y$. The arithmetic mean of $x$ and $y$ is 18, which means:\n\\[\n\\frac{x + y}{2} = 18\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives us:\n\\[\nx + y = 36\n\\]\nNext, we know that the geometric mean of $x$ and $y$ is $\\sqrt{92}$. The geometric mean is given by the square root of the product of $x$ and $y$, so:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{xy} = \\sqrt{92}\n\\]\nSquaring both sides gives us:\n\\[\nxy = 92\n\\]\nNow we have two equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx + y = 36 \\\\\nxy = 92\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nWe can solve for $x$ and $y$ using these two equations. First, we multiply the two equations to get:\n\\[\n(x + y)(x + y) = 36 \\cdot 36\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\nx^2 + 2xy + y^2 = 1296\n\\]\nWe know that $xy = 92$, so we substitute this into the equation:\n\\[\nx^2 + 2 \\cdot 92 + y^2 = 1296\n\\]\nSimplifying this gives us:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 + 184 = 1296\n\\]\nSubtracting 184 from both sides gives us:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = 1112\n\\]\nSo, the value of $x^2 + y^2$ is $\\boxed{1112}$.",
